From b697f84b18ac2733332986e9bb6d9bf596815986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Patel <shawn@almondbot.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:28:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] ootx: decode each base station through every device that
 sees it

The first device to report a station's sync pulses owned its only OOTX
decoder; bits from every other device were dropped. If that receiver kept
corrupting the slow OOTX stream (occluded, weak radio link) the station's
identity and calibration never decoded even while a second tracker
received it cleanly, and a disconnected owner left the decoder bound to a
freed device for good. Give each device its own decoder per station (the
first CRC-valid packet wins) and drop a device's decoders when it is
destroyed.
